---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Callout from "../components/Callout.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";

export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Cookie policy | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
  description="Which cookies this radiology and medicolegal law resource uses: strictly necessary storage, the single optional Google Analytics cookie, and how to accept, reject or change your choice."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Cookies"
    title="Cookie policy"
    description="One optional analytics cookie — set only if you accept it — and the strictly necessary storage that keeps the site working. Nothing else."
  />

  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Cookies"
    paragraphs={[
      "UK law requires consent before storing anything on your device that is not strictly necessary. This site therefore asks first: the banner offers Accept analytics or Reject analytics, and nothing optional is set until you choose.",
      "Your choice is remembered on your own device. You can change it at any time through the Cookie settings link in the footer, which re-opens the banner.",
    ]}
    contents={[
      { href: "#necessary", label: "Strictly necessary" },
      { href: "#analytics", label: "Optional analytics" },
      { href: "#choice", label: "Your choice" },
      { href: "#managing", label: "Managing cookies" },
    ]}
    reviewed="September 2026"
  />

  <section class="bg-white py-16">
    <div class="container-page">
      <div class="doc space-y-14">
        <Section id="necessary" index="01" eyebrow="Always on" title="Strictly necessary storage" lead="What the site needs to function. No consent is required, and it cannot be switched off.">
          <table class="mt-6 w-full border-collapse text-left">
            <thead>
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <th scope="col" class="border-b border-slate-300 px-3 py-3 font-sans text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-500">Name</th>
                <th scope="col" class="border-b border-slate-300 px-3 py-3 font-sans text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-500">Purpose</th>
                <th scope="col" class="border-b border-slate-300 px-3 py-3 font-sans text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-500">Expiry</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-800"><code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">ml-consent-v1</code> (localStorage)</td>
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-600">Remembers your cookie choice so the banner does not ask again. Not a cookie; nothing leaves your device.</td>
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-600">Until cleared</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-800">Clerk session</td>
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-600">Keeps you signed in to the secure login area only. Casual readers never receive it.</td>
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-600">Session</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-800">Cloudflare security</td>
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-600">Bot protection and load management set by the hosting platform.</td>
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-600">Short-lived</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </Section>
        <Section id="analytics" index="02" eyebrow="Optional" title="Analytics — only with consent" lead="A single Google Analytics 4 cookie, set only after you click Accept analytics.">
          <table class="mt-6 w-full border-collapse text-left">
            <thead>
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <th scope="col" class="border-b border-slate-300 px-3 py-3 font-sans text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-500">Name</th>
                <th scope="col" class="border-b border-slate-300 px-3 py-3 font-sans text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-500">Purpose</th>
                <th scope="col" class="border-b border-slate-300 px-3 py-3 font-sans text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-500">Expiry</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="bg-white">
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-800"><code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">_ga*</code></td>
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-600">Google Analytics 4: aggregate page-read counts. IP anonymised; 14-month retention.</td>
                <td class="border-b border-slate-200 px-3 py-3 align-top font-serif text-sm text-slate-600">Up to 2 years</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <Callout tone="key" title="Before you choose">
            <p>Until you accept, Google's tag loads in consent-denied mode: it cannot set cookies or send identifiers. Rejecting or ignoring the banner leaves it that way — the site works identically either way.</p>
          </Callout>
        </Section>
        <Section id="choice" index="03" eyebrow="Consent" title="How your choice works" lead="Withdrawing consent is as easy as giving it.">
          <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2.5 border-t border-slate-200 pt-4 font-serif text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
            <li><strong>Accept analytics</strong> — the _ga cookie may be set and page reads counted.</li>
            <li><strong>Reject analytics</strong> — nothing optional is set, and nothing is recorded.</li>
            <li><strong>Change your mind</strong> — the Cookie settings link in the footer re-opens the banner on any page.</li>
          </ul>
        </Section>
        <Section id="managing" index="04" eyebrow="Your browser" title="Managing cookies yourself" lead="Every browser also lets you control cookies directly.">
          <p class="mt-6 border-t border-slate-200 pt-4 font-serif text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-slate-600">You can block or delete cookies in browser settings at any time; the ICO guidance at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/for-the-public/online/cookies" class="underline decoration-slate-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-slate-900 hover:decoration-slate-600">ico.org.uk</a> explains how. Blocking strictly necessary storage may stop sign-in working, but reading the reference material is unaffected. Questions: see the <a href="/privacy-notice" class="underline decoration-slate-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-slate-900 hover:decoration-slate-600">privacy notice</a>.</p>
        </Section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
